<!--
  seed_data.xml (S4-D-20) - ODM 1.3 ClinicalData for 8 synthetic subjects
  (SS_001..SS_008) in study S_BJTDEMO / event SE_VISIT1.

  ALL DATA IN THIS FILE IS 100% SYNTHETIC. There are no real patients, no
  real PHI, and no real clinical measurements here - every value was invented
  for the biject clinical-trial demo.

  This dataset is DELIBERATELY MESSY. Four problems are planted across three
  distinct query types:
    1. Out-of-range value / decimal-shift typo   (SS_002 creatinine,
                                                  SS_007 hemoglobin)
    2. Cross-field mismatch                       (SS_004 weight vs BMI+height)
    3. Incomplete CRF / missing value             (SS_006 diastolic BP)

  RESOLVABILITY CONTRACT: every planted error is resolvable from OTHER fields
  seeded in this same dataset (source-note transcriptions, BMI+height, the
  composite BP reading). The demo agent derives each correction from seeded
  source data; it never has to invent a value. An XML comment directly above
  each planted error states (a) the error, (b) the query it should raise, and
  (c) the resolution source field.

  Subjects SS_001, SS_003, SS_005, SS_008 are clean controls (internally
  consistent, in-range) so the agent's "no action needed" path is exercised
  too. All OIDs match edc/study_def.xml exactly.

  Import mechanics: seed.py pushes this through the OpenClinica-ws SOAP
  importData operation subject-by-subject (comments are stripped before
  sending). UpsertOn + TransactionType="Insert" perform initial data entry;
  RangeChecks in study_def.xml are Soft, so out-of-range values land AND flag.
-->
